<p>NOTE:  Net income for the three months ended June 29, 1997, includes a $172 charge in cost of sales to reserve for first generation fibre channel boards in inventory, and a $270 income tax benefit related to a recovery under a tax sharing agreement with QLogic Corp. (a former subsidiary of the company which was spun off in February 1994).</p>
<p>Excluding these non-recurring items, net of tax, net income would have been $805, or 13 cents per share.  Net loss for the three months ended June 30, 1996, also includes a $750 income tax benefit related to the tax sharing agreement.  Excluding this non-recurring item, net loss would have been $1,304, or 22 cents per share.</p>
